{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529604-v5-homebrew-ritual-feedback-needed","id":1529604,"title":"(V5) Homebrew ritual feedback needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-28T10:40:35-08:00","id":1529604,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5) Homebrew ritual feedback needed","content":"Long story short, the first story of this chronicle I've just started involved a couple thin-blooded idiots trying to recreate From Marduk's Throat. How and why this is the case isn't terribly important, and a long story besides, but there's an outside chance the thin-bloods get <i>really</i> unlucky and pull it off. Meaning, I need to bang out mechanics for this just in case. This is what I have for starters, and any feedback would be very welcome.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Marmaduke's Throat (Level 5 Thin-blooded Alchemy ritual)</i></b><br /> <br /> Promised by a weird Mexican vampire as a cure to vampirism, this apparently ancient and powerful alchemical formula involves mixing together a bunch of plant poisons, animal venoms, and molten metals together...to apparently burn the vampirism right out of you or something? It's fucking weird but whatever, the Mexican dude seems cool, he just doesn't want to be a vampire (who does?) and needs a little help. This is why being a thin-blood is actually pretty dope compared to being a &quot;real&quot; vampire, other than being able to eat pizza, smoke weed, and go outside in daytime.<br /> <br /> Why it's named after a cartoon dog is anyone's guess. I put the name of this ritual in Google translate and that's what came out, so who am I to argue.<br /> <br /> <b>Ingredients:</b> The Alchemist's blood, empty Resonance blood, belladonna extract, ground castor beans, venom from a hemotoxic viper, recluse spider carcasses, molten gold, and mercury<br /> <br /> <b>Activation cost: </b>One Rouse check<br /> <br /> <b>Dice pools: </b>Resolve + Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> This ritual's effect varies by method.<br /> <br /> <b>Fixatio: </b>Each activation produces a single dose of poisoned vitae. Once five doses are produced and imbibed (by any vampire, not just the alchemist), the formula takes effect. The imbiber's Hunger drops to zero, and each turn after activation, the imbiber makes a Rouse check and a Resolve + Stamina test at difficulty 6. Failure on the Resolve + Stamina test results in one unhalved superficial damage per margin of failure. This process continues until the imbiber either enters torpor or reaches Hunger 5; during this time, the vampire can neither Blood Surge, mend damage, nor take any Physical action.<br /> <br /> If the imbiber enters torpor, they instead meet Final Death. If they reach Hunger 5, the outcome depends on the imbiber's generation. If the imbiber is 13th generation or below, their Blood Potency immediately increases by one. If the imbiber is a thin-blood (regardless of generation), their generation drops to 13th and they become a Caitiff with Blood Potency 1, with discipline dots as if they had been created Caitiff (two in one discipline of their choice, one in another, and a bonus dot as determined by Predator Type).<br /> <br /> <b>Calcinato:</b> The mortal used as the vessel for this formula immediately enters a comatose state upon the first activation roll, and makes a Stamina + Athletics test at difficulty 3 at the end of every night. If the mortal fails this test, they die and rise as a 13th generation wight with Potence 2 and Fortitude 2 (their Attributes and Skills are the same as the mortal's). If this formula is activated five times on the same mortal before they die, draining and killing them counts as having diablerized a 13th generation vampire with Potence 2 and Fortitude 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Athanor Corporis:</b> Known by witty vampires as &quot;the Darwin award&quot; or &quot;making yourself a snack&quot;, this is the riskiest but most beneficial method (including to anyone else) to brew this formula. Once this formula is activated five times by this method, the alchemist immediately enters torpor. At the beginning of each night, the alchemist does not make a Rouse check but rather automatically increases their Hunger by one and makes the Resolve + Stamina test described in the Fixatio method. Also as described in the Fixatio method, the alchemist cannot mend damage until this process is complete, and should the alchemist's health track be filled with Aggravated they meet Final Death.<br /> <br /> This continues until the alchemist reaches Hunger 5, at which point they become a 13th generation Caitiff as described in the Fixatio method, albeit still in torpor as per usual rules. However, if the alchemist is diablerized while still in torpor, they automatically fail their Resolve + Blood potency test to resist. Moreover, the alchemist counts as having one Blood Potency higher than their diablerist, as well as possessing Fortitude 3, Presence 3, and Potence 3, for purposes of spending experience to raise these traits through diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T06:32:09-08:00","id":1558185,"title":"","content":"Wasn't <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/pt/title/tt0068284/\" target=\"_blank\">Blacula </a>named that in fact? No, no, wait, Mamuwalde was his true name, my bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T15:51:55-08:00","id":1558195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529604-v5-homebrew-ritual-feedback-needed#post1529604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why it's named after a cartoon dog is anyone's guess. I put the name of this ritual in Google translate and that's what came out, so who am I to argue.</div> </div> </div> </div>This made me laugh out loud.<br /> <br /> As far as mechanics go, I like the general idea. I'd maybe do the disciplines and required blood slightly differently. Instead of empty resonance, maybe use a resonance and you can put your 2 and 1 point into the disciplines available from that resonance. Those disciplines would also be the ones that someone diablerizing the alchemist/mortal could choose from, as opposed to flat Potence, Fortitude, and Presence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T14:12:38-08:00","id":1558220,"title":"","content":"I'd say more needs to be consumed. Some versions of the ritual had you required to drink the pool of the gen you wanted to become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T11:40:38-07:00","id":1562130,"title":"","content":"I think it has a number of problems at least from how I'd run such a thing. I understand where the decisions come from, but personally would change the following, for the given reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. I'd put all consequences in the Activation roll. There's a lot of rolling for the sake of rolling. If something between rolls could alter them I'd see a point, but the way it's now, I see no point.<br /> <br /> 2. Seriously, killing PCs for the sake of it isn't fun. They went all the way to get this ritual, just for it to be lethal with nothing to be done about it? Pure RNG? As given that's an average 10 rolls at Diff 6 without any means to increase the Pool. A topped character will get 1 damage per roll in average, already going 2 Agg into an 8 levels Health Track by the end. Why? I'd put them in Torpor and no new tries are possible, and still not make it so damn impossible after they already have everything in place.<br /> <br /> 3. On the other hand, no Disciplines, period. I'd give the player the XP for everything Thin Blood they lost, but no Disciplines at first. Disciplines are heavily trained and starting 13th Gen have them to signify at least 5 years of undeath. The ex-Thin Blood should need time and effort to buy anything.<br /> <br /> 4. I'd let the character keep their Alchemy dots and recipes as a record. They can't use it, but they can teach other Thin Bloods if they want.<br /> <br /> 5. I'd consider adding the ingredients of From Marduk's Throat: Blood from Vampires of the target Blood Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}